Patch summary:
Installs an arm64-v8a-only multiArch app on an x86_64 device with ARM
translation. For a multiArch app that targets Android 15 or later, the
package manager picks the ABI from the natively supported ABIs only, which
leave out the ABIs a native bridge translates, so Google Play's arm64-only
multiArch apps were refused with
INSTALL_FAILED_MULTI_ARCH_NOT_MATCH_ALL_NATIVE_ABIS.
The 64-bit list now has the native ABIs first and the translated ones after
them: an app with x86_64 libraries still installs as x86_64. The 32-bit list
stays native only, as a translated entry would fail every multiArch app
without 32-bit libraries. Applies after frameworks-base-native-bridge.patch.
DSA (desktop-subsystem-for-android) makes the same change in its
frameworks/base patch 0004.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
index 93792c9..82f5cdb 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
@@ -340,7 +340,24 @@ final class PackageAbiHelperImpl implements PackageAbiHelper {
             return sNativelySupported64BitAbis;
         }
 
-        sNativelySupported64BitAbis = getNativelySupportedAbis(Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS);
+        // Ika: a multiArch app that targets Android 15 or later picks its ABI from this list
+        // only, and a 64-bit ABI the native bridge translates was left out, so an app with
+        // arm64-v8a libraries alone was refused with
+        // INSTALL_FAILED_MULTI_ARCH_NOT_MATCH_ALL_NATIVE_ABIS although the translator runs it
+        // like any other arm64-v8a app. The native ABIs still come first, so an app that has
+        // them is installed with them; the translated ones follow. 32-bit ABIs stay native
+        // only: listing a translated one would make every multiArch app without 32-bit
+        // libraries fail the match.
+        final List<String> abis = new ArrayList<>();
+        for (String abi : getNativelySupportedAbis(Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS)) {
+            abis.add(abi);
+        }
+        for (String abi : Build.SUPPORTED_64_BIT_ABIS) {
+            if (!abis.contains(abi)) {
+                abis.add(abi);
+            }
+        }
+        sNativelySupported64BitAbis = abis.toArray(new String[0]);
         return sNativelySupported64BitAbis;
     }
 
